// `Sched::expand` of lib/_tests/native/runtime/runtime_held_index_tests.hthr
// on its own, for scripts/bench-probes' `omega/sched-expand` case: a
// `runtime fn` loop over an array, each word from the third on the sum of
// the two before it, with three index proofs found by `bv_omega`. What the
// case measures is the generator's found proofs: omega's reflection, and the
// substitution reducer under its reduce-and-name step
// (issues/small-step-reducer-on-computed-terms.md). A copy, because `--only`
// does not reach a declaration of a module that also holds expected refusals.
